viewport: unknown zoom: 1.00 natural
ok: nodes=37 edges=30 flows=10 direction=lr theme=gruvbox
canvas: 5 diagrams on one canvas, drawn whole at 100%
diagram l0 "L0 · System context" at 0,7: extent=118x20 nodes=8 edges=7 routes=7
  description: System context: the machine manager is one box. The control plane and humans + mmctl call it; it drives the bare-metal providers, boots and audits the machines, keeps images and diagnostics in S3, and alerts in Slack. Nothing inside is shown yet, so L1 opens it.
diagram l1 "L1 · The machine manager" at 0,34: extent=173x25 nodes=11 edges=9 routes=9
  description: L0's box opened one level: its boundary services — private gRPC, webapi, provider registry, cluster reconcile, SSH + BMC ops and the boot server — sit in the Machine manager box, while the control plane, humans, providers, machines and S3 stay outside it.
diagram l1b "L1b · The machine side" at 0,66: extent=130x17 nodes=7 edges=4 routes=4
  description: The fleet end of the same system. Bare-metal machines run the machine-agent, which registers and heartbeats into public gRPC inside the manager's box; the River queue uploads diagnostics to S3 and webapi confirms actions in Slack, both outside. The fleet drives these outward relations.
diagram l2 "L2 · Inside — queue and dispatch" at 0,90: extent=147x15 nodes=6 edges=6 routes=6
  description: Inside the box, first slice: requests land on the River queue, which dispatches provision jobs to the provider registry, audit work to SSH + BMC ops and diagnostic events to the janitor; the janitor proposes actions back to webapi. L2b carries the state writes this slice leaves out.
diagram l2b "L2b · Inside — the state writes" at 0,112: extent=59x22 nodes=5 edges=4 routes=4
  description: Inside the box, second slice: the writes into the Postgres state store — job rows from the queue, machine rows from private gRPC, machine state from public gRPC heartbeats and cluster state from the reconcile loop. Same box, same manager; only the state edges are drawn here.
